        <briefdescription>
<para>Asynchronous allocation of memory. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>This method asynchronously allocates <computeroutput>*s</computeroutput> bytes on the specified memory node. Upon success, <computeroutput>*ptr</computeroutput> will contain the address of the allocated buffer. If the allocation fails, <computeroutput>*s</computeroutput> will contain a negative value.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>ctx</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Untyped backend context </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>memory_node</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Memory node where the allocation should occur </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>s</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Pointer to the size of the allocation </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>prereqs</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>List of events that should finish before the allocation starts </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
